WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.790
The price barely moved and I didn't close. Why is my balance lower?

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.412
Besides trading fees, perpetual contracts usually have a funding mechanism.

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:17.962
When the rate is positive, longs usually pay shorts. When it's negative, it flips.

00:00:17.962 --> 00:00:21.070
It's not a fixed interest everyone pays to the exchange.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:48.614
Say the position value at settlement is 1,000 and the rate is 0. 01%. This fee is 0.

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:53.690
10. It's based on the position value, not your first 100 of margin.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.763
The interval and the rate can change by pair, platform and market.

00:01:26.763 --> 00:01:30.276
Don't remember it as 'every contract, every eight hours, forever'.

00:01:30.276 --> 00:01:33.150
And don't treat receiving funding as risk-free income.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.160
The last level is practice only.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:02.384
First explain what you're trading and which direction.

00:02:02.384 --> 00:02:06.265
Then check the mode, size, margin, auto-add, exit plan and costs.

00:02:06.265 --> 00:02:11.160
If you don't understand one item, pause. Don't guess your way through the buttons.

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:28.790
I know how to do it, and I know this risk isn't right for me. So I won't.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:33.476
That's a passing result too. Finishing the course doesn't mean you can make money.

00:02:33.476 --> 00:02:34.920
Understand first, then act.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:45.673
Whatever you trade, fees are a cost that adds up. Compare fees on NexuAlpha,

00:02:45.673 --> 00:02:50.910
and register through an official partner link with our code to get part of your fees back.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:52.190
Lower cost, same risk.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.271
You've finished both seasons.

00:02:54.271 --> 00:02:58.100
Pick the episode that felt hardest, and rewatch it before you ever trade.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:00.730
Understand first, then act.
